	"description" : "Chill paper dune background with day and night, set it yourself or let it follow your PC clock ^^\n\n[h2]Settings[/h2]\n[list]\n[*][b]Follow PC clock[/b]: the time of day follows your PC.\n[*][b]Time of day[/b]: pick it yourself (0 = night, 50 = sunset, 100 = noon).\n[*][b]Plant[/b]: branch, dune grass, pampas or none.\n[*][b]Plant size[/b]: how big the plant is (0 = no plant).\n[*][b]Wind[/b]: how much the plant moves (0 = still).\n[*][b]Tempo[/b]: how fast everything moves (0 = still).\n[*][b]Rise and fall[/b]: how much the dunes go up and down.\n[*][b]Roll sideways[/b]: how fast the dunes slide along.\n[*][b]Curve height[/b]: how tall the curves are.\n[*][b]Number of curves[/b]: how many curves fit on screen.\n[*][b]Sun size[/b]: size of the sun and moon.\n[*][b]Sun height[/b]: how high they sit.\n[*][b]Sand lines[/b]: the fine lines on the front dunes (0 = off).\n[*][b]Dust[/b]: the specks in the air (0 = off).\n[/list]\nBrightness, contrast and colour are in Wallpaper Engine's own colour options. The frame rate follows its FPS setting.\n\n[h2]Video[/h2]\nhttps://youtu.be/-LcWhYW59Ko",
